<article class="type-lab">
  <p class="type-lab__kicker">DESIGN LAB / ORIGINAL TYPE EXPERIMENT / 0.1</p>
  <h1>Ken Cartridge Display</h1>
  <p class="type-lab__intro">An original angular uppercase face with a continuous width axis. The narrow and wide drawings share a construction, while stem thickness stays steady and the counters and diagonal angles change. It is a working specimen, not a replacement for the site’s current fonts.</p>
  <div class="type-lab__controls" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <label for="type-width">Width: <output id="type-width-value" for="type-width">85</output></label>
    <input type="range" id="type-width" min="65" max="115" value="85" step="1" aria-describedby="type-width-help">
    <div class="type-lab__range-ends"><span>65 / condensed</span><span>115 / expanded</span></div>
    <p id="type-width-help">This controls the font’s real <code>wdth</code> axis. It does not stretch the rendered text with a CSS transform.</p>
    <label for="type-text">Try a headline</label>
    <input type="text" id="type-text" value="MAKE IT MAKE SENSE." maxlength="140" aria-describedby="type-coverage">
    <p id="type-coverage">Uppercase A–Z, numbers and the punctuation shown below. Lowercase input is displayed as uppercase. Accents and other characters use the fallback face.</p>
    <p id="type-font-status" role="status">Loading the local prototype font…</p>
  </div>
  <p class="type-lab__sample type-lab__hero" id="type-live">MAKE IT MAKE SENSE.</p>
  <section class="type-lab__row" aria-labelledby="type-real-headlines">
    <h2 id="type-real-headlines">In the site’s voice</h2>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">Platforms. Content. People.</p>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">Ideas in circulation</p>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">One shared truth for Storybook and Figma</p>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">Let’s make something work.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="type-lab__row" aria-labelledby="type-coverage-heading">
    <h2 id="type-coverage-heading">Coverage and awkward neighbours</h2>
    <p class="type-lab__proof">ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ<br>0123456789<br>. , : ; ! ? ( ) [ ] ' ’ ‘ “ ” " - – — / + = &amp; # * … ↗</p>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">AV AW AT TA TO VA WA YA LT LY FA</p>
    <p class="type-lab__sample">B8 G6 O0 P9 Q R S5 M N W</p>
  </section>
  <section class="type-lab__row type-lab__notes" aria-labelledby="type-limits">
    <h2 id="type-limits">What needs another pass</h2>
    <p>The angular bowls, pointed joins and square terminals are intentional. This first cut needs optical refinement, more kerning pairs, accent coverage and review across browsers before it becomes a site font. The ampersand and small punctuation are especially provisional. There is one drawn weight and no weight, slant or optical-size axis.</p>
    <p>Body copy, interface controls and code continue to use IBM Plex. Display headings elsewhere still use Anton.</p>
    <p><a href="/assets/kh-font/ken-display/KenCartridgeDisplay-Variable.woff2">Download variable WOFF2</a> · <a href="/assets/kh-font/ken-display/KenCartridgeDisplay-Variable.ttf">Download variable TTF</a> · <a href="/assets/kh-font/ken-display/OFL.txt">SIL Open Font License</a></p>
  </section>
</article>
<script>
(() => {
  const lab = document.querySelector('.type-lab');
  const width = document.getElementById('type-width');
  const value = document.getElementById('type-width-value');
  const text = document.getElementById('type-text');
  const live = document.getElementById('type-live');
  width.addEventListener('input', () => {
    lab.style.setProperty('--type-axis', width.value);
    value.value = width.value;
  });
  text.addEventListener('input', () => { live.textContent = text.value || 'MAKE IT MAKE SENSE.'; });
  document.fonts.load('400 48px "Ken Cartridge Display"', 'MAKE IT MAKE SENSE.').then(fonts => {
    document.getElementById('type-font-status').textContent = fonts.length ? 'Local variable font loaded. Width axis: 65–115; default: 85.' : 'The prototype font did not load; you are seeing the fallback.';
  }).catch(() => {
    document.getElementById('type-font-status').textContent = 'The prototype font did not load; you are seeing the fallback.';
  });
})();
</script>
